/P 223 0 R
/E (Urban roads face potholes, damaged infrastructure, waterlogging, traffic congestion, accidents, hit-and-run, rash driving, and vulnerable-pedestrian risks, while authorities rely mainly on fixed CCTV, manual inspections, and public complaints. Bus cameras are largely underused, causing delayed hazard/incident detection, incomplete coverage, inefficient maintenance, and increased road-safety risks.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
